    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Eliphaz Accuses: Job Does Not Fear God"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Should a wise man answer with windy knowledge,",
          "and fill his belly with the east wind?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Should he argue in unprofitable talk,",
          "or in words with which he can do no good?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But you are doing away with the fear of God",
          "and hindering meditation before God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For your iniquity teaches your mouth,",
          "and you choose the tongue of the crafty."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your own mouth condemns you, and not I;",
          "your own lips testify against you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Are you the first man who was born?",
          "Or were you brought forth before the hills?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have you listened in the council of God?",
          "And do you limit wisdom to yourself?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What do you know that we do not know?",
          "What do you understand that is not clear to us?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Both the gray-haired and the aged are among us,",
          "older than your father."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Are the comforts of God too small for you,",
          "or the word that deals gently with you?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why does your heart carry you away,",
          "and why do your eyes flash,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "that you turn your spirit against God",
          "and bring such words out of your mouth?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What is man, that he can be pure?",
          "Or he who is born of a woman, that he can be righteous?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behold, God puts no trust in his holy ones,",
          "and the heavens are not pure in his sight;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "how much less one who is abominable and corrupt,",
          "a man who drinks injustice like water!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“I will show you; hear me,",
          "and what I have seen I will declare"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "(what wise men have told,",
          "without hiding it from their fathers,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "to whom alone the land was given,",
          "and no stranger passed among them)."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The wicked man writhes in pain all his days,",
          "through all the years that are laid up for the ruthless."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Dreadful sounds are in his ears;",
          "in prosperity the destroyer will come upon him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He does not believe that he will return out of darkness,",
          "and he is marked for the sword."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He wanders abroad for bread, saying, ‘Where is it?’",
          "He knows that a day of darkness is ready at his hand;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "distress and anguish terrify him;",
          "they prevail against him, like a king ready for battle."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Because he has stretched out his hand against God",
          "and defies the Almighty,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "running stubbornly against him",
          "with a thickly bossed shield;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "because he has covered his face with his fat",
          "and gathered fat upon his waist"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and has lived in desolate cities,",
          "in houses that none should inhabit,",
          "which were ready to become heaps of ruins;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "he will not be rich, and his wealth will not endure,",
          "nor will his possessions spread over the earth;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "he will not depart from darkness;",
          "the flame will dry up his shoots,",
          "and by the breath of his mouth he will depart."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him not trust in emptiness, deceiving himself,",
          "for emptiness will be his payment."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It will be paid in full before his time,",
          "and his branch will not be green."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He will shake off his unripe grape like the vine,",
          "and cast off his blossom like the olive tree."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the company of the godless is barren,",
          "and fire consumes the tents of bribery."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They conceive trouble and give birth to evil,",
          "and their womb prepares deceit.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
